Raise the Ray head CPU limit in the upstream e2e tests from 500m to 1.

Applied by scripts/kuberay-compat.sh to the kuberay v1.7.0 checkout before running the suites.

With the default kubelet cpuCfsQuota=true, a 500m limit throttles the head during startup.
On slower cores (e.g. Standard_D4s_v3) the head exits with "Module MetricsHead failed to
start. Timeout after 30.0 seconds." and crash-loops, failing most rayjob, mtls and
rayservice tests. The request stays 300m and KubeRay still generates --num-cpus=1, so only
the throttling ceiling changes. Drop this patch once upstream raises the limit.

diff --git a/ray-operator/test/e2erayservice/testdata/locust-cluster.burst.yaml b/ray-operator/test/e2erayservice/testdata/locust-cluster.burst.yaml
index a6d1b03..225c3b0 100644
--- a/ray-operator/test/e2erayservice/testdata/locust-cluster.burst.yaml
+++ b/ray-operator/test/e2erayservice/testdata/locust-cluster.burst.yaml
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ spec:
                 cpu: "300m"
                 memory: "1G"
               limits:
-                cpu: "500m"
+                cpu: "1"
                 memory: "2G"
             ports:
               - containerPort: 6379
